00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:17,320
Last time we spoke about the difference between apoptosis and necrosis.

00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:25,020
While apoptosis is a conservation or a recycling of all the genetic material, all the cellular

00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:33,980
material and necrosis is basically the destruction of the cell, usually always pathological in the

00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:34,980
necrosis.

00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:42,340
Apoptosis can be pathological, but usually we think of it as a normal physiological response

00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:50,020
where necrosis is not a normal physiological response per se, you can say it's a normal physiological

00:00:50,020 --> 00:00:57,740
response in the event of an enemy attack, but it is destruction.

00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:00,820
So why does apoptosis take place?

00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:02,380
Why is this so important?

00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:06,700
Well, there are normal physiological reasons for apoptosis.

00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,540
It's normal in prudence.

00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:14,060
So if anybody has ever had a garden or apple trees or fruit trees, if you don't prude

00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:20,460
your garden, if you don't take care of it in that way, you're never going to have a good

00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:27,660
crop of apples, you have to prude your garden, you have to pick the weeds, you have to take

00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:30,420
care of it in order to grow a good crop.

00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:37,260
So there is prudence that takes place from a neurological perspective, from a braid science

00:01:37,260 --> 00:01:38,260
perspective.

00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:44,260
So if you talk about your neurons get pruned, your neurons work on a use it or lose it

00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:46,660
basis, so do your muscle cells.

00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:51,700
If you don't use them, your body sees them as an important eduille, they will go through

00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:54,980
apoptosis and be destroyed, they're not needed.

00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:59,460
So you have to use your body in order to keep those cells.

00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:07,300
Also, there are certain tissues that are hormone-dependent tissues, like endometrial tissues, women's

00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:15,620
rest post lactation after they have a baby, there's an infiltration of new cells for making

00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:22,980
a milk after the baby's done lactating, those cells go through apoptosis and are destroyed.

00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,020
There's no need for them.

00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:32,140
During a normal cycle, a woman's cycle goes through the endometrial tissue, goes through proliferation

00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:34,900
and apoptosis.

00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:39,580
So that's a normal process, a normal physiological process.

00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:45,380
It's a way to get rid of those cells that are not needed anymore.

00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:51,020
Cells that are necessary during development that aren't necessary after development go through

00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,620
apoptosis.

00:02:52,620 --> 00:03:03,940
So again, apoptosis is the way to recycle cells that aren't needed for that person's

00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:12,500
well-being at this point, so the example would be specific T cells and auto antigen and bone

00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:18,100
marrow cells go through apoptosis after they've served their purpose.

00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:24,740
It really all cell lines, not every cell line, both your heart cells don't go through apoptosis,

00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:29,740
but most your cell lines, once they reproduce, go through apoptosis.

00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:34,100
It has been said that you have a brand new body, which isn't completely true, but for

00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:41,660
the most part, you do have a brand new body and both cell lines, every about 12 to 24 weeks

00:03:41,660 --> 00:03:47,660
as those cells reproduce another cell, and the mother cell, you could say, dies.

00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,660
It goes through apoptosis, your body gets rid of it.

00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:53,460
You just have too many cells in your body.

00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:59,580
So we reproduce a new cell in order for it to do its job and the old cell dies.

00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:02,100
That is normal apoptosis.

00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:06,540
There are some pathological reasons that you go through apoptosis.

00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:11,820
Any severe damage to the cell is going to cause the cell to die.

00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:17,300
So this could be purposeful, and let's say if somebody goes through radiation or chemotherapy

00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:24,900
in a purposeful attempt to kill a cell that is in rapid replication, that is a cancer cell,

00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:31,120
but the problem is, is you damage any cell with radiation or chemotherapy, and you risk

00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:34,260
it going through apoptosis.

00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:35,260
That's just what happens.

00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:39,060
That's the negative side of radiation and chemotherapy, is you're not just killing cancer

00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,900
cells, you're killing every cell.

00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,300
So not a good thing.

00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:45,500
But there's other pathological reasons.

00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:50,420
If there's thermal injury or if you go through a time where there's no oxygen to the cell,

00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:57,080
any damage that's going to occur to the DNA, the endoplasmic reticulum, a viral infection

00:04:57,080 --> 00:05:04,980
because remember viruses go inside the cell, and your immune system can recognize that there's

00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:09,420
a virus inside the cell by a little receptor that comes out of the cell, right, and the

00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:17,180
immune system can destroy that cell and basically gobble it up, and hence doing it kills the virus.

00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,620
That's how your body will kill a virus.

00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:26,860
Also, if a tumor suppressor gene is activated, you know, we talk a lot about the tumor suppressor

00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:33,620
genes in our cancer series, and those are very important because those are the genes that

00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:37,900
can become deactivated when somebody has cancer.

00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:45,260
So a tumor suppressor gene is a gene that turns on the apoptosis cycle, and we'll talk more

00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:53,900
about that in our later weeks here about apoptosis, but tumor suppressor genes turn on apoptosis.

00:05:53,900 --> 00:06:00,860
When a person has cancer, the problem is tumor suppressor genes are turned off or disabled,

00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:07,220
or a person has a genetic trait where they don't have certain tumor suppressor genes.

00:06:07,220 --> 00:06:13,500
So when a tumor suppressor gene is activated or turned on, it activates apoptosis, excuse

00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,500
me.

00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:23,860
It is usually only turned on when there is rapid replication, so that is the body's defense

00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,340
against cancer.

00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:29,580
So you have cancer that's starting to grow in your body, tumor suppressor genes.

00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:35,260
In this picture, the P53 gene, which is a very important tumor suppressor gene, stimulates

00:06:35,260 --> 00:06:39,500
apoptosis, and helps kill that cancer.

00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:42,220
So apoptosis is important.

00:06:42,220 --> 00:06:46,700
There's pathological reasons for apoptosis, the person has cancer and the tumor suppressor

00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:53,460
genes turned on, a viral infection, any stress to the cell, any damage to the cell, and there's

00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:55,740
normal physiological reasons.

00:06:55,740 --> 00:07:02,260
So that's the way your body cleans up itself and keeps your body healthy, and it sells that

00:07:02,260 --> 00:07:05,340
once they reproduce, they go through apoptosis.

00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:11,980
And that's what's broken, this cycle of apoptosis, that's the first thing that's broken in

00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,980
order for a person to get cancer.

00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:18,780
You can't have cancer unless apoptosis is not taking place.

